In `GitHubInstallation.dispatch`, the sender/authenticated-user check is only performed in the path where an ACTIVE `Integration` already exists and `installations_exist` is false:
```py
integration = Integration.objects.get(external_id=installation_id, status=ObjectStatus.ACTIVE)
if pipeline.fetch_state("github_authenticated_user") != integration.metadata["sender"]["login"]:
    return error(...)
```
But in the earlier branch where `Integration.objects.get(external_id=installation_id)` raises `Integration.DoesNotExist`, the code immediately does:
```py
except Integration.DoesNotExist:
    ret
